cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "receptor-resurfacing-pipeline: de novo resurfacing of plant immune receptor binding sites"
abstract: >-
  A Nextflow workflow that redesigns the binding surface of a plant immune
  receptor so it recognises a chosen effector. It takes a docked
  receptor-effector complex, or two monomers it places with a
  constraint-driven pose solver, rebuilds the receptor surface around the
  effector pose with RFdiffusion, assigns sequence with ProteinMPNN, and
  scores the candidates with Rosetta, Boltz-2 and AlphaFold3. Negative
  steering of the Boltz-2 predictions is delegated to
  structure-negative-steering. Applied to the integrated HMA decoy domain of
  the rice NLR Pikp-1 against the Magnaporthe oryzae MAX effectors AVR-PikF,
  AVR-Pia, PWT3 and PWT7.
authors:
  - family-names: Williams
    given-names: Joshua
    email: joshuandwilliams@outlook.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/joshuandwilliams/receptor-resurfacing-pipeline"
keywords:
  - de novo protein design
  - RFdiffusion
  - ProteinMPNN
  - plant immunity
  - NLR
  - MAX effector
  - Nextflow
